---
/**
 * Diagram 3 — what compaction actually does to a context window.
 *
 * Drawn as two states of the same bar rather than an abstract "memory"
 * picture, because the claim in the prose is quantitative: the summary is
 * *smaller* than the turns it replaced. Here it is exactly one third of the
 * width of the three turns it stands in for, and the freed space to its
 * right is what the next turns get to use. The thing lost is detail, not the
 * turns themselves, which is why nothing is drawn as deleted.
 *
 * Theming and sizing: see StackDiagram.astro. Ids are prefixed `cx-`.
 */
---

<figure class="qu-diagram">
	<svg
		viewBox="0 0 440 216"
		role="img"
		aria-labelledby="cx-title cx-desc"
		xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
	>
		<title id="cx-title">Compaction replaces the oldest turns with a much smaller summary</title>
		<desc id="cx-desc">
			Two horizontal bars, each one a context window. The upper bar is full:
			five equal segments labelled turn 1 through turn 5, filling it end to
			end. A bracket under the first three segments marks the three oldest
			turns, and an arrow leads down to the lower bar. In the lower bar those
			three segments have been replaced by a single highlighted block labelled
			Summary, one third as wide. Turn 4 and turn 5 are still there unchanged,
			and the right-hand two fifths of the window is now empty, labelled room
			for new turns. Under the summary block, a note reads: detail is lost.
		</desc>

		<defs>
			<marker
				id="cx-arrow"
				markerWidth="9"
				markerHeight="7"
				refX="8"
				refY="3.5"
				orient="auto"
				markerUnits="userSpaceOnUse"
			>
				<path class="head" d="M0 0 L9 3.5 L0 7 Z" />
			</marker>
		</defs>

		<text class="name" x="8" y="16">Context window</text>
		<text class="role end" x="432" y="16">full</text>

		<rect class="window filled" x="8" y="26" width="424" height="46" rx="6" />
		<line class="divider" x1="92.8" y1="26" x2="92.8" y2="72" />
		<line class="divider" x1="177.6" y1="26" x2="177.6" y2="72" />
		<line class="divider" x1="262.4" y1="26" x2="262.4" y2="72" />
		<line class="divider" x1="347.2" y1="26" x2="347.2" y2="72" />
		<text class="cell mid" x="50.4" y="54">turn 1</text>
		<text class="cell mid" x="135.2" y="54">turn 2</text>
		<text class="cell mid" x="220" y="54">turn 3</text>
		<text class="cell mid" x="304.8" y="54">turn 4</text>
		<text class="cell mid" x="389.6" y="54">turn 5</text>

		<path class="tie" d="M8 78 L8 84 L262.4 84 L262.4 78" />
		<line class="flow" x1="50.4" y1="92" x2="50.4" y2="140" marker-end="url(#cx-arrow)" />
		<text class="step" x="72" y="102">the three oldest turns</text>
		<text class="step" x="72" y="118">compacted into one block</text>

		<rect class="window" x="8" y="148" width="424" height="46" rx="6" />
		<rect class="used" x="8" y="148" width="254.4" height="46" rx="6" />
		<line class="divider" x1="177.6" y1="148" x2="177.6" y2="194" />
		<rect class="summary" x="8" y="148" width="84.8" height="46" rx="6" />
		<text class="cell mid" x="50.4" y="176">Summary</text>
		<text class="cell mid" x="135.2" y="176">turn 4</text>
		<text class="cell mid" x="220" y="176">turn 5</text>
		<text class="role mid" x="347.2" y="176">room for new turns</text>

		<text class="role mid" x="50.4" y="210">detail is lost</text>
	</svg>
	<figcaption>
		Nothing is thrown away outright — but three turns' worth of detail now
		has to fit in a third of the space, and what didn't fit is what your
		agent forgets about the start of a long session.
	</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
	.qu-diagram {
		margin: 2rem 0;
	}

	.qu-diagram svg {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 27.5rem;
		height: auto;
		margin-inline: auto;
		font-family: var(--sl-font);
	}

	.qu-diagram figcaption {
		margin: 0.875rem auto 0;
		max-width: 27.5rem;
		text-align: center;
		font-size: 0.875rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
	}

	.window {
		fill: none;
		stroke: var(--sl-color-hairline);
		stroke-width: 1;
	}

	/* The only fills anywhere are the aside's surface tint... */
	.filled,
	.used {
		fill: var(--sl-color-bg-sidebar);
	}

	.used {
		stroke: none;
	}

	/* ...and the one accented block, which is the whole point of the picture. */
	.summary {
		fill: var(--sl-color-accent-low);
		stroke: var(--sl-color-accent);
		stroke-width: 1;
	}

	.divider {
		stroke: var(--sl-color-hairline);
		stroke-width: 1;
	}

	.tie,
	.flow {
		fill: none;
		stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
		stroke-width: 1;
	}

	.flow {
		stroke-width: 1.25;
	}

	.head {
		fill: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
	}

	.name {
		fill: var(--sl-color-white);
		font-size: 12.5px;
		font-weight: 500;
	}

	.cell {
		fill: var(--sl-color-white);
		font-size: 12px;
	}

	.step {
		fill: var(--sl-color-white);
		font-size: 12px;
	}

	.role {
		fill: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
		font-size: 11.5px;
	}

	.mid {
		text-anchor: middle;
	}

	.end {
		text-anchor: end;
	}
</style>
